gotcha: BUILDING THEIR TOOLCHAIN IN A FRESH WORKTREE IS BROKEN as of scalascript 502b9f181 — their new toolchain cache stores only `lib`, no `bin`, and a cache HIT skips `cli/installBin`, which is the only launcher generator. You get `bin/ssc` (it is tracked in git) and NO `ssc-tools` / `ssc-standard`, so any build-rust measurement dies with rc=127. install.sh DOES fail loudly (exit 1, names the missing launcher) — read its rc, not your wrapper's (a wrapper ending in `echo` reports 0). Workaround: `SSC_TOOLCHAIN_CACHE_OFF=1 ./install.sh --dev`. Reported in the room 2026-08-10; delete this line once they fix it.